diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 340640b..de404a1 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -25,3 +25,10 @@
 - Moderator big screen lives at `/moderate/games/:id` (`Moderate::GamesController`, layout `screen`) and uses `rqrcode` (`RQRCode::QRCode`) to render the join link QR code as an inline `<svg>`.
 - Player flow lives at `/play/:code` (`PlayController`) and never renders `correct` / `is-correct` in HTML or ActionCable payloads while a question is open.
 - Live updates use `GameChannel` (authorized via signed `ActiveSupport::MessageVerifier` tokens) and `GameBroadcaster` (`async` adapter in `config/cable.yml`), paired with `live_screen_controller.js` / `live_play_controller.js` that sync state on WebSocket connect/reconnect/`visibilitychange`/`online` and fall back to `/state` JSON polling if WebSocket is disconnected on flaky conference Wi-Fi.
+
+## Scoring, Leaderboard & Prizes (Release 3)
+- `Quiz` (`winners_count`, default `3`, integer `>= 1`) is exposed in quiz settings as "Number of winners" and snapshotted onto `Game#winners_count` when a game is created.
+- `GameQuestion#opened_at` is recorded when each question opens (`start!` / `next_question!`), and `Answer#answered_at` is updated on every `submit_answer!` call so answer duration reflects the player's last pick.
+- `Game#leaderboard` ranks players by points descending, then total elapsed time of correct answers ascending (ignoring wrong answers), then join order (`created_at, id`). Points are never rendered to players while a question is open or closed.
+- After "End quiz" (`finished`), the moderator big screen displays `<ol class="leaderboard">` with place, name, points (`pluralize(points, "point")`), and "Top N" / "Draw" / "Reset winners" controls; each player's phone displays `"Place X of Y"`, points, and `"You won!"` if marked `winner`.
+- `Game#pick_top_winners!`, `Game#draw_winners!`, and `Game#reset_winners!` update `Player#winner` inside `Game#with_lock`, increment `Game#winners_revision` (included in `state_version` so repeated draws push live updates), and broadcast via `GameBroadcaster.broadcast_winners` to both the big screen and individual player channels.
